{"id": "DfMobCBRPgo", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why did Parshurama's father order him to kill his own mother? 4 sons refused. 1 obeyed. And then he did something nobody expected. 🪓💔\n\nThe sage Jamadagni and his wife Renuka had five sons. Rama, the youngest, would one day be called Parshurama.\n\nOne day, while her sons were out gathering fruit, Renuka went to the river to bathe. There she saw King Chitraratha playing in the water with his queen, a garland of lotuses around his neck. For one moment, her heart wandered.\n\nShe came home shaking. The sage saw it in her face. \"DHIK!\" Shame!\n\nHe ordered his four elder sons, one by one: \"Kill your mother.\" Rumanvan, Sushena, Vasu and Vishvavasu stood silent. His curse took their minds.\n\nThen Rama came home. \"Kill your mother, son, and do not grieve.\" He obeyed.\n\nHis father's anger vanished. \"What you did was hard, my son. Ask for any boon.\" And Rama used those boons to undo everything: bring my mother back to life, let her never remember it, heal my brothers.\n\nShe woke up smiling. She never knew. 🙏\n\n📖 Source: Mahabharata, Vana Parva 3.116 (verses 1–18), the story as the sage Akritavrana tells it to Yudhishthira.\n\nThis is Part 3 of our Parshurama series. Every part stands on its own, so start anywhere!\n\n📚 The Navadurga Set, kids' picture books on the nine forms of Maa Durga, is out now at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n💬 4 sons refused. 1 obeyed. WHO WAS RIGHT? Tell us in the comments 👇\n🔁 Share it with someone who has never heard this story.\n📌 Save it for later.\n\n#parshurama #parashurama #renuka #jamadagni #vishnuavatar #dashavatar #mahabharata #hindumythology #sanatandharma #indianmythology #hindustories #mythologystories #rishikatha #jaiparshuram", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793532807, "like_count": 23559, "comment_count": 231, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": 