 her, abandon her, not kill her.", "timestamp": 1794211884, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "tripaathhii", "author_id": "76360942743", "id": "18224348761346644", "text": "So women are calling this misogyny! 😭💔🙏🏻But ignore the fact a married woman thought about something like that with another man ?? Isn't that cheating.", "timestamp": 1794210647, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "shivakumarpj.29", "author_id": "46752919595", "id": "17912964861312474", "text": "Pithru vaakya paripalana", "timestamp": 1794190471, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "the_missing_candidate", "author_id": "49649986358", "id": "18124199461941135", "text": "Parshuram knew that his father has ability to bring her back that's the reason he done this", "timestamp": 1794023060, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "r1.kaizen", "author_id": "44769469657", "id": "18069227831523372", "text": "I mean if he didn’t obey then may be his father would curse him too and did what he wanted to and would never bring her back… so may be in order fix everything Parshurama Ji did what he had to and it worked his father was no more angry… so after his father asked what he wanted and parshuram just asked to fix everything one by one… so was not about right or wrong but rather a smart decision ( only he knows how he felt ) 👍", "timestamp": 1793887931, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "bat176", "author_id": "12736893521", "id": "18033248456683442", "text": "All are stories to guide humanity thats it nothing real", "timestamp": 1793883167, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "phantom_0360", "author_id": "7199574447", "id": "18147225832577870", "text": "Yk this is all bullshit,? Now if suppose parshuram did it and his father couldn't bring his mother back what would have happened then? See whatever scenario you see it from he was wrong as well as his egoistic father no.matter how big of rishi he was", "timestamp": 1793831102, "like_count": 18}, {"author": "dy.lan290", "author_id": "8917999068", "id": "17895122043614301", "text": "🙏🙏", "timestamp":